<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-NORWAY'S STIANSEN WINS MEN'S SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-NORWAY'S STIANSEN WINS MEN'S SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tom Stiansen of Norway won the men's slalom gold medal at the Alpine skiing world championships on Saturday in a total time of one minute 51.70 seconds, according to unofficial results.  </p>
<p>Sebastien Amiez of France took the silver in 1:51.75 and</p>
<p>Alberto Tomba of Italy the bronze in 1:52.14.</p>
